  "id": "phagocytosis",
  "term": "phagocytosis",
  "definition": "Phagocytosis is a receptor-mediated process in which phagocytic cells move toward pathogens, recognize and bind them, take them inside, and then mature the internal compartment so the target can be destroyed. In the source packet, it is described as an important part of innate immune clearance and as unfolding through an ordered series of stages.",
